{#-
  A driver's links: one box each, because they are two different offers. The ambassador
  brings somebody in and takes a share; the driver link brings in a project they will
  manage, and it can carry a discount. One box holding both read as a single form with two
  buttons, which is not what it is.

  Both send `POST /links`, which renders this tab again with the link shown. Not an address
  with the percentage in it: the address ends up in the browser's history and in whatever
  log sits in front of us, and this address is a thing that pays somebody — the same reason
  the sso's session token travels as a ticket.

  `links.made` is what was just generated, when this page is the answer to one of the two
  buttons. It is shown inside the box it came from, so a driver who pressed one of them does
  not have to work out which link they are looking at.
-#}
<section class="link-box card">
  <div class="card-head">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.ambassador") }}</div>
  <div class="link-box-body">
    <p class="link-hint">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.ambassador_hint") }}</p>
    <form class="link-form" method="post" action="/links">
      <input type="hidden" name="kind" value="ambassador">
      <button class="btn" type="submit">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.make") }}</button>
    </form>
    {%- if links.made and links.made.kind == "ambassador" %}
    {% set made = links.made %}
    {% include "partials/link_made.njk" %}
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>

{%- if links.driver %}
<section class="link-box card">
  <div class="card-head">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.driver") }}</div>
  <div class="link-box-body">
    <p class="link-hint">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.driver_hint") }}</p>
    <form class="link-form" method="post" action="/links">
      <input type="hidden" name="kind" value="driver">
      <label class="field">
        <span class="field-label">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.discount") }}</span>
        <select class="input" name="percentage">
          <option value="">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.discount_none") }}</option>
          {%- for percentage in links.percentages %}
          <option value="{{ percentage }}">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.percentage", { percentage: percentage }) }}</option>
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
      </label>
      <button class="btn" type="submit">{{ t("projects_hub.driver.links.make") }}</button>
    </form>
    {%- if links.made and links.made.kind == "driver" %}
    {% set made = links.made %}
    {% include "partials/link_made.njk" %}
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
